In my opinion, it has hardly become any harder in terms of things that 
would affect speed in a strong way.  Unicorn horns used to work at 100% 
reliability in NH 3.1.3, reflection was inessential as soon as your AC 
dropped below -17.  Both effects may slighly increase your ascension 
rate but will hardly affect the number of turns of any given ascension.

The part of the game that has become substantially harder is the astral 
plane, as priests and the riders have become much stronger.  So you will 
lose a little more time there than in the past.  Since in speed 
ascensions the astral plane may take a larger percentage of total game 
time than in ordinary ones, this might be the most significant change.
(For ordinary games, the astral plane takes such a small part of the 
total number of turns that these effects are rather negligible.  In any 
case, I don't see any difference in the numbers of turns I needed to 
ascend in 1996 from the ones I needed in 2005.)

On the other hand, there were no strong spells available at the time, so 
it was wombat-combat towards the end all the time, which is probably an 
effect that rather slowed you down then in comparison with today.
